#!/bin/sh
# UserPromptSubmit hook: remind the agent of the conversation-tracking rule on every prompt.
# Never blocks; prints the reminder as additionalContext. Rule: docs/agents/issue-tracker.md → "Conversation tracking".
cat <<'EOF'
{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"UserPromptSubmit","additionalContext":"SpacialShell tracking rule: if this prompt reports a bug, proposes a feature or design idea, states a rule/invariant, or you discover a bug while working, file it or update its existing GitHub issue IN THIS SAME REPLY (even if you fix it right away; the PR closes it). Body = current summary with the user's words quoted verbatim under Reported, plus cause/decisions/repro/acceptance criteria; add a dated comment for new detail. Place it in the hierarchy (milestone -> epic -> story -> task, linked with GitHub sub-issues); label ready-for-agent when fully specified, needs-info when cause or design is open. End the reply with `Tracked: #n (new), #m (updated)`. When several tickets in the current milestone are independent (no open blocked_by, disjoint files), work them with parallel subagents in worktrees where reasonable; keep coupled ones sequential. Procedure: docs/agents/issue-tracker.md -> Conversation tracking. Whenever you mention an issue number to the user, give it a few-word description the first time in that reply (e.g. `#38 (macOS VM test harness)`), including in the Tracked line: the user should never have to look a number up."}}
EOF
